DAY 08 — LINUX SECURITY BASICS
Commands Reference Sheet
Machine: Kali Linux | User: raven
==========================================

--- SPOTTING SUID/SGID IN PERMISSIONS ---
ls -la <file>                    # look for 's' instead of 'x' in owner/group slot
                                  # -rwsr-xr-x  = SUID set (owner slot)
                                  # -rwxr-sr-x  = SGID set (group slot)

--- FINDING SUID BINARIES ---
find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null           # all SUID binaries (system-wide)
find / -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null | wc -l   # count how many exist
find /usr/bin -perm -4000 -type f 2>/dev/null    # limit search to /usr/bin only

--- FINDING SGID BINARIES ---
find / -perm -2000 -type f 2>/dev/null           # all SGID binaries (system-wide)

--- REMOVING SUID/SGID (only if you know what you're doing) ---
sudo chmod u-s <file>             # remove SUID bit
sudo chmod g-s <file>             # remove SGID bit

--- WORLD-WRITABLE FILE CHECK (revisited from Day 02) ---
find / -perm -002 -type f 2>/dev/null            # world-writable files, system-wide
find / -perm -002 -type f 2>/dev/null | grep -v "^/proc"   # exclude noisy /proc results

--- BASIC SSH HARDENING CHECK ---
sudo grep "PermitRootLogin" /etc/ssh/sshd_config       # is direct root login allowed?
sudo grep "PasswordAuthentication" /etc/ssh/sshd_config # is password login allowed?

--- OCTAL VALUES FOR SPECIAL BITS ---
4000 = SUID
2000 = SGID
1000 = Sticky bit
chmod 4755 <file>    # sets SUID + rwxr-xr-x

